# Deep Learning & Real-World Scenarios

Full guide: [`DEEP_LEARNING_STANDARD.md`](../../DEEP_LEARNING_STANDARD.md). Complements `principal-engineer-mastery.mdc`.

## When editing topic notes

- **Expand the authoritative file** — do not create a second HashMap/VT doc with the same facts.
- **Stop writing cheat sheets.** Teach: problem → naive → break → concept → internals → production → failure → interview → Principal decision.
- Every major topic needs **≥2 production scenarios**, **when NOT to use**, failure investigation, and Interviewer Mode (Basic→Principal + follow-up).
- Internals: Level 1 simple → Level 2 technical → Level 3 JVM → Level 4 production.
- Nuance: never “HashMap is always O(1)” / “VT are faster” / “parallel streams improve performance” without workload caveats.
- Illustrative numbers must be labeled **Illustrative example.**
- Cross-link the chain (e.g. HashMap → equals/hashCode → CHM → memory → GC → performance).

## Scenario lab

Investigation exercises live in `scenario-lab/` — do not spoil root cause before the investigation section.

## Priority order for deep passes

Collections → Concurrency → Virtual Threads → JVM → GC → Streams → Performance → then other chapters.
